  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Part of the Hippodrome beach, in Cagnes-sur-Mer, is reserved for dogs: the town presents it as their swimming area, between groyne 1 and groyne 2, at the boundary with Villeneuve-Loubet. It is the only beach in the town listed for dogs.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The area is the one indicated by the town of Cagnes-sur-Mer ("Cagnes-sur-Mer, friend of animals" page) and by the Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office. On the leash, the two sources do not say the same thing: the tourist office states that dogs may be off-leash but must not be left unsupervised or disturb other users, whereas the town publishes no rule specific to the beach. When in doubt, keep your dog on a leash. We found no official source on possible seasonal restrictions or on a shower at this spot.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: this is a good stop between Nice and Villeneuve-Loubet if you're combining several dog-friendly spots in one day.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Plage de Vaugrenier in Villeneuve-Loubet is a few minutes away by car.</p>
    </div>

